            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 7 changed paths in full for the risk lens and found no reachable exploit caused by this candidate.",
              "engine/review/gitexec/gitexec.go: revisions are passed to rev-parse after --end-of-options, and are suffixed with ^{commit}. Argument vectors are composed in code and no shell is involved, so there is no command injection or option injection through a revision. The real-git tests also check that '--all' and '-x' are refused.",
              "engine/review/gitexec/gitexec.go: gitEnvironment removes every GIT_* variable and LC_ALL before git starts, so GIT_DIR, GIT_CONFIG_*, GIT_EXTERNAL_DIFF and GIT_DIFF_OPTS cannot redirect or alter the digest. The diff also passes --no-ext-diff and --no-textconv, and takes its attributes from the empty tree, so a candidate .gitattributes cannot select a user-configured diff driver that runs code.",
              "engine/review/gitexec/gitexec.go: AddWorktree sets core.hooksPath to the null device, so no repository hook runs on checkout, and realgit_test.go checks this against a real post-checkout hook. Worktree uses Lstat and does not follow symlinks, and it refuses a path that is not a worktree of the same repository.",
              "The error text quotes git's stderr, but clip bounds it to 2000 bytes. I found no secret exposure.",
              "The unpinned $GIT_DIR/info/attributes and the zlib dependence are documented in gitexec.go and README.md. A digest mismatch fails closed, so it does not weaken the integrity binding.",
              "engine/architecture_test.go, engine/reviewresult/reviewresult.go and odd/review-results/README.md only change ring registration, comments and documentation, and add no behavior that touches security."
            ]
          }
        }
