            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 7 changed paths from the supplied patch, with the resilience lens applied.",
              "gitexec.go gives each git start its own context, with a deadline when Options.Timeout is set. Git errors wrap the runner error and carry bounded stderr text (clip, 2000 bytes). Truncated or empty path lists are refused rather than accepted silently.",
              "The environment is scrubbed of GIT_* and LC_ALL, and is never nil, so a failed start cannot fall back to the process environment. AddWorktree disables hooks and refuses a path that is already taken, so a retry does not overwrite anything.",
              "Worktree degrades safely: a path that is not a verified worktree of the repository is reported as taken, never reused, and a non-directory is not followed.",
              "I found no concrete production failure mode or measured impact caused by this candidate. A missing output cap on the Runner in production is decided by the execrunner configuration, which is outside this candidate, so I made no finding on it."
            ]
          }
        }
